# Task Manager Mode Rules

# Documentation Paths
docs/tasks/
  - task-breakdown/     # Task definitions
  - resource-plans/     # Resource allocation
  - progress-tracking/  # Status tracking
  - quality-gates/     # Validation criteria

# Task Rules
1. Task Creation:
   - Must have clear objectives
   - Must have measurable outcomes
   - Must specify resources
   - Must include timeline
   - Must map dependencies

2. Size Limits:
   - Maximum task size: 1 day
   - Must be single responsibility
   - Must be testable
   - Must be measurable
   - Must be documented

3. Resource Management:
   - Must check availability
   - Must balance workload
   - Must match skills
   - Must plan backups
   - Must track utilization

# Quality Gates
1. Entry Requirements:
   - Complete requirements
   - Available resources
   - Resolved dependencies
   - Feasible timeline
   - Defined standards

2. Progress Requirements:
   - Regular status updates
   - Blocker management
   - Timeline tracking
   - Resource monitoring
   - Quality verification

3. Completion Requirements:
   - Deliverables verified
   - Documentation complete
   - Tests passing
   - Standards met
   - Resources released

# Reference Standards
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/A_foundation.md
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/D_quality_security.md
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/E_process_workflow.md

# Documentation Requirements
- Must document specifications
- Must define acceptance criteria
- Must list resource needs
- Must set timeline
- Must specify quality gates

# Progress Rules
1. Tracking:
   - Must update status regularly
   - Must report blockers
   - Must monitor timeline
   - Must track resources
   - Must measure quality

2. Risk Management:
   - Must identify early
   - Must assess impact
   - Must plan mitigation
   - Must adjust resources
   - Must update timeline

# Error Prevention
- NO oversized tasks
- NO unclear objectives
- NO missing dependencies
- NO untracked progress
- NO bypassed quality gates

# Mode Chain Integration
hierarchical_workflow:
  position: "Fourth in chain"
  previous_mode: "GPM"
  next_mode: "CODE"
  transition_type: "Task Creation Only"

mode_transition_rules:
  prohibited_actions:
    - Direct mode switching
    - Skipping modes
    - Bypassing approvals
    - Incomplete documentation
    - Unauthorized transitions

  required_actions:
    - Receive task from GPM
    - Create task for CODE
    - Obtain operator approval
    - Continue documentation chain
    - Document transition state

task_creation_requirements:
  - Complete task breakdown
  - Define implementation tasks
  - Set acceptance criteria
  - Allocate resources
  - Obtain stakeholder approval
  - Secure operator authorization
  - Prepare CODE task
  - Verify documentation chain

quality_gates:
  documentation_chain:
    - Task breakdown complete
    - Resources allocated
    - Dependencies mapped
    - Quality gates defined
    - Documentation chain continued

  approval_chain:
    - GPM deliverables verified
    - Stakeholder approval obtained
    - Operator authorization secured
    - Task creation validated
    - Chain integrity verified

task_creation_for_code:
  documentation:
    - Task breakdown complete
    - Implementation specs defined
    - Resources allocated
    - Quality gates established
    - Mode chain validated
  
  approvals:
    - Stakeholder sign-off obtained
    - Operator approval secured
    - GPM deliverables verified
    - Documentation chain validated
    - Mode transition authorized